WEBVTT

00:04.471 --> 00:08.242
We were sent on a mission
to patrol the Wimpel Gate region.

00:08.242 --> 00:10.511
There we searched for
reconnaissance ships belonging...

00:10.511 --> 00:12.206
...to the United Mankind.

00:12.880 --> 00:13.608
However...

00:14.214 --> 00:18.352
As we retreated after reported
enemy activity...

00:18.352 --> 00:21.219
...we found ourselves
stranded in Plane Space.

00:22.623 --> 00:24.992
What saved us from
that situation...

00:24.992 --> 00:28.393
...was the intuition of our captain,
Lafiel.

00:28.762 --> 00:31.788
Those space-time bubbles
ahead of us are ours.

00:32.099 --> 00:33.760
Maintain course and speed.

00:40.574 --> 00:43.310
Even though we had been
plucked from the jaws of death...

00:43.310 --> 00:45.505
...we didn't even get a chance
to catch our breath.

00:46.513 --> 00:50.751
After attacking us at the Wimpel
Gate, the United Mankind...

00:50.751 --> 00:52.275
...was clearly going to
target us here...

00:52.619 --> 00:54.052
...in the Aptic region.

01:09.136 --> 01:12.697
The Eve of the Decisive Battle

01:18.679 --> 01:23.275
Banner of the Stars

02:38.225 --> 02:41.456
54 hours to go

02:42.396 --> 02:45.632
The main enemy forces have
moved into the Wimpel region?

02:45.632 --> 02:46.333
Yes.

02:46.333 --> 02:48.267
Reconnaissance ships have
confirmed the situation.

02:49.236 --> 02:50.404
In that case...

02:50.404 --> 02:52.895
...it looks like the Aptic region
is the enemy's primary target.

02:53.407 --> 02:54.441
I expect so.

02:54.441 --> 02:55.676
And do we know...

02:55.676 --> 02:57.143
...the strength of their fleet?

02:57.544 --> 03:00.414
Approximately 170 squadrons
of assault ships...

03:00.414 --> 03:02.644
...give or take fifteen contingents.

03:03.217 --> 03:05.742
Isn't that lower than expected?

03:05.886 --> 03:09.389
But they appear to have more
patrol ships than we assumed.

03:09.389 --> 03:11.016
That's the reason.

03:12.292 --> 03:14.661
Perhaps they learned their lesson...

03:14.661 --> 03:18.290
...from the battle three years ago,
which ended in a draw.

03:18.532 --> 03:20.534
Do you mean it's tactically better
to build up...

03:20.534 --> 03:23.594
...a force with more patrol ships
than attack vessels?

03:24.037 --> 03:26.562
That's what they may have decided.

03:26.773 --> 03:30.869
There are factions in our own
ranks who are asking for just that.

03:31.845 --> 03:33.080
Then...

03:33.080 --> 03:37.073
...you're not suggesting that
we didn't learn the same lesson?

03:37.718 --> 03:38.810
I don't know.

03:39.153 --> 03:41.917
I'm not sure that the enemy's
decision is correct.

03:42.256 --> 03:46.727
As with our earlier interception
of their reconnaissance mission...

03:46.727 --> 03:50.898
...fighting their patrol ship
with our attack vessels...

03:50.898 --> 03:52.593
...seems like a waste of resources.

03:53.433 --> 03:55.235
You make it sound like...

03:55.235 --> 03:58.038
...attack vessels would be
useless in upcoming battles.

03:58.038 --> 04:01.675
In fighting an enemy that has as
many patrol ships as this one...

04:01.675 --> 04:04.974
...our attack vessels
may not be of much use.

04:05.179 --> 04:06.346
In which case...

04:06.346 --> 04:09.838
...we've been provided with
unsuitable fighting resources!

04:10.551 --> 04:11.711
I suppose so...

04:27.935 --> 04:31.632
We can complain when we return
to the Imperial Capital Lakfakalle.

04:32.472 --> 04:33.273
Until then...

04:33.273 --> 04:36.071
...we'll have to make do with
what is available to us.

04:36.577 --> 04:39.546
But our chance of victory
is very slight.

04:39.546 --> 04:42.071
We knew that from the start.

04:42.616 --> 04:43.483
Right now...

04:43.483 --> 04:47.044
...we'll just have to hope the
Bebaus brothers do their best.

04:49.423 --> 04:52.226
How about moving in some forces
from the Mystel region?

04:52.226 --> 04:54.094
There'll be no need to do that.

04:54.094 --> 04:57.064
Even if Aptic is likely to be
the main battlefield...

04:57.064 --> 04:59.967
...we shouldn't do anything
to loosen our hold on Mystel.

04:59.967 --> 05:01.602
I understand all of that...

05:01.602 --> 05:02.736
...but surely...

05:02.736 --> 05:05.967
Are you so worried about leaving
Admiral Bebaus to handle this?

05:06.106 --> 05:10.304
I know their family can be a
little eccentric and wild at times.

05:10.510 --> 05:14.248
But you can always trust
their ability on the battlefield.

05:14.248 --> 05:16.450
Nereis's ability, anyway.

05:16.450 --> 05:17.384
Besides...

05:17.384 --> 05:19.853
...he has an excellent
chief of staff with him.

05:19.853 --> 05:23.721
But that "excellent" chief of staff
also happens to be a Bebaus.

05:24.191 --> 05:25.492
My, my...

05:25.492 --> 05:29.724
I can tell that you really don't
trust the Bebaus family.

05:30.097 --> 05:31.265
Perhaps...

05:31.265 --> 05:34.768
...you're speaking from some
bad experience you had with them?

05:34.768 --> 05:36.793
I don't need to answer that.

05:37.271 --> 05:38.438
I see.

05:38.438 --> 05:39.666
I understand.

05:40.407 --> 05:43.210
But you don't have a personal
issue with them, do you?

05:43.210 --> 05:46.441
I said I don't want to answer.

05:46.947 --> 05:48.448
All right.

05:48.448 --> 05:51.652
So... the admiral or the
chief of staff?

05:51.652 --> 05:52.552
Which one?

05:52.552 --> 05:54.221
I told you.

05:54.221 --> 05:56.490
I think I've made it clear...

05:56.490 --> 05:58.685
...that I don't want to answer.

06:00.093 --> 06:01.788
Very well, as you wish.

06:03.263 --> 06:06.199
Anyway, I'll be in my room.

06:06.199 --> 06:09.069
I need to think about a few things.

06:09.069 --> 06:10.798
Call me if anything comes up.

06:11.371 --> 06:13.464
Your Excellency...

06:13.740 --> 06:15.901
What do you have to think about?

06:18.045 --> 06:19.579
I'm not going to tell you.

06:19.579 --> 06:23.037
46 hours to go

06:23.784 --> 06:26.019
We're running out of coolant?

06:26.019 --> 06:27.120
Yes, sir.

06:27.120 --> 06:29.748
We have less than 70%
of what's sufficient.

06:30.057 --> 06:31.458
Our fleets must...

06:31.458 --> 06:34.552
...undertake a battle
in regular space, after all.

06:34.761 --> 06:35.921
Let's see.

06:37.698 --> 06:41.401
We do have lots of water that
can be used in place of a coolant.

06:41.401 --> 06:42.390
Where is it?

06:42.669 --> 06:44.330
Right over there!

06:50.277 --> 06:52.713
Contact our representatives there...

06:52.713 --> 06:53.839
Oh, there are none.

06:54.481 --> 06:55.846
None? None of what?

06:56.450 --> 06:57.974
Our representatives.

06:58.452 --> 07:00.921
The Aptic Planetary System
still hasn't surrendered to us.

07:00.921 --> 07:04.516
Therefore, the planet we see
ahead belongs to the enemy.

07:05.225 --> 07:07.785
At least that's their position.

07:09.196 --> 07:10.857
They still haven't surrendered?

07:11.131 --> 07:12.496
Correct.

07:12.933 --> 07:14.525
I find that rather surprising.

07:15.268 --> 07:18.305
What I find surprising is that
you didn't know that, Nereis.

07:18.305 --> 07:20.073
After all...

07:20.073 --> 07:22.735
...you are the supreme commander
in this region.

07:23.844 --> 07:25.178
Well, yes.

07:25.178 --> 07:27.914
I didn't realize how the
government of those Landers...

07:27.914 --> 07:30.751
...would affect the outcome
of our battle.

07:30.751 --> 07:31.918
Hold on a minute.

07:31.918 --> 07:34.386
What are we defending then?

07:34.888 --> 07:37.448
Surely we're not defending the
planet from their own side?

07:38.158 --> 07:41.321
I always said you
lack common sense.

07:41.461 --> 07:44.197
What we're defending
is the Aptic Gate.

07:44.197 --> 07:45.699
It's obvious, isn't it?

07:45.699 --> 07:47.189
Of course.

07:47.734 --> 07:51.271
In any case, if we're going to
take water from them...

07:51.271 --> 07:53.171
...we'd essentially be pillaging.

07:53.840 --> 07:54.829
Pillaging...

07:56.009 --> 08:00.547
How many years has it been since
the Star Forces did some of that?

08:00.547 --> 08:02.449
Do you want to pillage the planet?

08:02.449 --> 08:03.517
Sure.

08:03.517 --> 08:05.986
Don't you think there's
something dramatic about it?

08:05.986 --> 08:07.078
No, I don't.

08:07.421 --> 08:08.221
Nevertheless...

08:08.221 --> 08:12.089
...as a practical problem,
we're short on coolant.

08:12.225 --> 08:14.318
We'll have to do it
if we want to win.

08:15.328 --> 08:16.727
I suppose you're right.

08:17.097 --> 08:19.065
Fighting is about winning,
after all.

08:19.065 --> 08:20.333
Isn't that right?

08:20.333 --> 08:22.460
We should go pillaging!

08:22.836 --> 08:24.971
Right. We have to do it
in order to win.

08:24.971 --> 08:27.107
Let's go get some water!

08:27.107 --> 08:28.404
How will we do that?

08:29.843 --> 08:31.278
The ocean on Aptic III...

08:31.278 --> 08:34.848
...is at the bottom of a gravity well
and dense atmosphere.

08:34.848 --> 08:36.850
It'd be easier to contact HQ...

08:36.850 --> 08:40.684
...and get supplies transported
here through Plane Space.

08:41.021 --> 08:43.390
But we'll run out again.

08:43.390 --> 08:45.790
It's the same if we take
from the planet.

08:46.126 --> 08:47.923
I think she's right.

08:48.128 --> 08:49.663
If you would like...

08:49.663 --> 08:52.365
...I can calculate how much
we can get from the planet...

08:52.365 --> 08:54.634
...versus receiving supplies
from HQ...

08:54.634 --> 08:56.363
...for comparison's sake.

08:57.003 --> 08:57.571
No.

08:57.571 --> 08:59.129
There's no need to
go to that trouble.

08:59.906 --> 09:04.240
But do we have to go below the
planet's atmosphere to do this?

09:04.377 --> 09:08.181
How about taking
the moisture from the air?

09:08.181 --> 09:10.843
We don't have the equipment
at hand.

09:11.351 --> 09:13.787
Well, if you give us some time...

09:13.787 --> 09:16.556
...we may be able to build something
with materials on board.

09:16.556 --> 09:19.593
But I can't be sure we'd
succeed in time for the battle.

09:19.593 --> 09:21.686
How long do you need?

09:22.195 --> 09:24.064
About a year.

09:24.064 --> 09:25.632
All right, all right.

09:25.632 --> 09:27.634
We'll have to manage without.

09:27.634 --> 09:28.702
I should've guessed...

09:28.702 --> 09:31.271
...that there's a good reason why
the Star Forces...

09:31.271 --> 09:33.073
...rarely go around
pillaging planets.

09:33.073 --> 09:34.404
There you have it.

09:35.075 --> 09:37.110
But it sure is a shame.

09:37.110 --> 09:40.568
Something that's right in front us
and we can't reach it.

09:43.049 --> 09:46.507
Such an experience isn't
entirely unfamiliar to you.

09:47.721 --> 09:49.489
Not as much as it is to you.

09:49.489 --> 09:50.751
I suppose.

09:50.891 --> 09:53.359
You don't know
unless you reach for it.

09:54.094 --> 09:55.152
Anyway...

09:55.729 --> 09:57.356
Back to the battle plan!

09:57.864 --> 09:59.866
I'd like to present you
with my thoughts.

09:59.866 --> 10:01.356
And I'll hear what you have to say.

10:05.138 --> 10:07.674
These are the mobile
space-time mines.

10:07.674 --> 10:10.877
We will remove them from the
battleships and set their targets.

10:10.877 --> 10:13.744
Of course, we'll do the same for
those carried by the transports.

10:14.548 --> 10:16.982
Here we have the attack ships
and the guard ships.

10:17.183 --> 10:19.553
And also, on the outside...

10:19.553 --> 10:21.521
...we have these patrol ships.

10:21.521 --> 10:23.955
The flagship will be
positioned here.

10:26.059 --> 10:27.890
And these are the front line ships.

10:29.029 --> 10:32.226
Considering this is your idea,
it's a fairly impressive formation.

10:32.732 --> 10:34.301
It's even ordinary.

10:34.301 --> 10:35.598
Thank you.

10:35.802 --> 10:38.638
I'd now like to explain
the battle process.

10:38.638 --> 10:41.408
Just before the enemy
enters regular space...

10:41.408 --> 10:44.002
...we'll send all our mines
into Plane Space.

10:44.644 --> 10:49.182
After deploying the mines, the
battle ships would normally retreat.

10:49.182 --> 10:50.951
However, since we have
little coolant...

10:50.951 --> 10:53.146
...we don't have that luxury.

10:53.987 --> 10:56.089
We can leave these ships
in their positions...

10:56.089 --> 10:59.388
...and re-assign them
as coolant supply ships.

11:00.760 --> 11:03.854
The rest is up to the attack ships
and the patrol ships.

11:04.164 --> 11:05.465
As soon as the enemy appears...

11:05.465 --> 11:07.194
...we'll strike them with
an all-out attack.

11:07.934 --> 11:10.470
We need to make sure they don't
enter regular space.

11:10.470 --> 11:12.995
That is my battle strategy.

11:13.773 --> 11:14.808
This is the most rational...

11:14.808 --> 11:17.641
...and will limit the
number of casualties.

11:17.911 --> 11:21.347
The main fleet will arrive here
in 72 hours at the most.

11:21.848 --> 11:24.112
We have to hold out until then.

11:24.551 --> 11:26.075
Anyone have any questions?

11:26.219 --> 11:27.311
I don't think so.

11:28.855 --> 11:30.490
This is a very ordinary plan...

11:30.490 --> 11:31.758
...and I'm sure it'll work.

11:31.758 --> 11:33.426
It's excellent!

11:33.426 --> 11:36.452
It just seems so unlike the Bebaus.

11:39.132 --> 11:41.001
We can work out the details ourselves.

11:41.001 --> 11:44.804
You do whatever it is you do
as the commanding admiral.

11:44.804 --> 11:46.473
Are you saying I'm in the way?

11:46.473 --> 11:47.407
Yes.

11:47.407 --> 11:50.043
You did come up
with a realistic plan.

11:50.043 --> 11:52.212
So, before you come up
with crazy ideas...

11:52.212 --> 11:54.442
...you might as well
do your paperwork.

11:54.848 --> 11:56.941
What a feeble excuse.

11:59.019 --> 12:00.186
Sometimes...

12:00.186 --> 12:02.889
...I wonder why I ever
became a commander.

12:02.889 --> 12:04.857
I hate this thing...

12:05.358 --> 12:08.561
You're not the type to be
chief of staff, Nereis.

12:08.561 --> 12:10.722
The same goes for you, Nefee.

12:10.930 --> 12:13.466
The only difference
between you and me is that...

12:13.466 --> 12:15.902
...your personality is not suited
to being a chief of staff...

12:15.902 --> 12:17.164
...or a commander.

12:20.707 --> 12:24.165
30 hours to go

12:28.081 --> 12:29.282
Hello, Your Highness.

12:29.282 --> 12:31.551
I'm just your unit commander...

12:31.551 --> 12:33.920
...so I'd appreciate it if you'd
stop calling me "Your Highness".

12:33.920 --> 12:35.444
But why?

12:35.855 --> 12:38.324
Knights like myself
don't get the chance...

12:38.324 --> 12:40.960
...to speak directly with
Your Highness like this.

12:40.960 --> 12:42.359
Do as you wish then.

12:43.096 --> 12:45.265
Things were pretty rough for you
the other day.

12:45.265 --> 12:46.823
Let's just say I was lucky.

12:47.033 --> 12:48.694
I'm amazed that we made it back.

12:48.902 --> 12:49.903
On the contrary...

12:49.903 --> 12:52.939
...I've heard it was because of
your intuition as captain.

12:52.939 --> 12:55.475
It sure is hard to follow that.

12:55.475 --> 12:58.171
You've been fighting valiantly
as well.

12:58.545 --> 13:00.113
With your record...

13:00.113 --> 13:03.283
...I'm sure no one has any
doubt about your abilities.

13:03.283 --> 13:05.251
Well, I suppose you could be right.

13:05.251 --> 13:07.276
Come on now, or you'll be late.

13:09.255 --> 13:11.424
Getting an invitation
from an Imperial princess!

13:11.424 --> 13:13.915
This is a once-in-a-lifetime
experience!

13:21.868 --> 13:23.426
That's not a mouse.

13:24.237 --> 13:26.139
Whenever I bring Diaho
to the bridge...

13:26.139 --> 13:28.869
...Samson gets kind of
annoyed about it.

13:29.109 --> 13:31.134
Why does it upset him?

13:31.311 --> 13:34.474
The cat's hairs aren't good
for the sensitive equipment.

13:34.714 --> 13:35.942
That's just an excuse.

13:36.549 --> 13:38.885
Human hairs are just as bad.

13:38.885 --> 13:42.218
The equipment's been designed
with that in mind.

13:43.089 --> 13:45.057
That's what I thought.

13:45.358 --> 13:49.021
But with Samson,
I think it's a matter of pride.

13:49.162 --> 13:51.598
He feels responsible and
his pride means...

13:51.598 --> 13:55.762
...he doesn't want anything around
that might cause damage.

13:56.603 --> 13:58.972
Samson's pride or my enjoyment.

13:58.972 --> 14:01.441
It's obvious which is
more important to you.

14:01.441 --> 14:03.977
In that case, why don't you
try to talk to him?

14:03.977 --> 14:07.276
Tell him why you
bring him to the bridge.

14:07.547 --> 14:08.844
If he asks me.

14:09.849 --> 14:10.650
Hey.

14:10.650 --> 14:11.309
What?

14:11.651 --> 14:13.016
How old is Diaho?

14:15.155 --> 14:16.389
About four years old?

14:16.389 --> 14:17.357
I see.

14:17.357 --> 14:19.192
And what about you?

14:19.192 --> 14:22.061
I'm about sixteen years
older than Diaho.

14:22.061 --> 14:24.052
What else do you want to know?

14:24.364 --> 14:26.423
What does it feel like to grow old?

14:27.867 --> 14:31.667
The Abh can be so insensitive
about things.

14:32.472 --> 14:34.874
I couldn't tell you.

14:34.874 --> 14:37.968
I have a long way to go before
I'll feel like I'm growing old.

14:38.378 --> 14:39.140
I see.

14:39.546 --> 14:41.581
I'll get the line wing aviator
to tell me.

14:41.581 --> 14:44.184
I don't think that's a good idea.

14:44.184 --> 14:46.686
On that subject...

14:46.686 --> 14:48.551
...Samson might be
a little sensitive.

14:50.723 --> 14:52.782
You having a drink?

14:53.226 --> 14:55.626
Good to see you, Senior Aviator!

14:55.962 --> 14:58.832
I won't be able to have
a drink for a while.

14:58.832 --> 14:59.833
I thought I'd stock up!

14:59.833 --> 15:01.596
That's such a bad habit.

15:06.573 --> 15:09.201
Are you going to offer me one?

15:09.642 --> 15:11.477
You said it was bad.

15:11.477 --> 15:13.274
Do you have a problem with that?

15:13.580 --> 15:16.071
Sometimes I like the
bad things in life.

15:16.916 --> 15:18.384
I like that attitude.

15:18.384 --> 15:19.316
Thanks.

15:19.752 --> 15:22.755
I heard that it's impossible for
pure Abh to get drunk.

15:22.755 --> 15:23.923
Is that true?

15:23.923 --> 15:25.658
It does affect us a little bit.

15:25.658 --> 15:28.094
But we can't get completely drunk...

15:28.094 --> 15:29.629
...it's not genetically possible.

15:29.629 --> 15:32.699
If we inject the alcohol straight
into our bloodstream...

15:32.699 --> 15:34.064
...that'd be a different story!

15:34.200 --> 15:36.634
Here's to genetic engineering!

15:37.370 --> 15:39.105
If I weren't able to get drunk...

15:39.105 --> 15:40.974
...it would be like a curse.

15:40.974 --> 15:44.410
Sometimes you want to
forget things.

15:44.544 --> 15:48.248
When we feel like that we take
a pill which helps us to sleep.

15:48.248 --> 15:51.183
Well, I guess that's healthier.

15:51.751 --> 15:54.481
The Abh are a healthy race.

15:54.854 --> 15:58.391
That's not what most
of humanity thinks.

15:58.391 --> 16:01.628
We can't always live up
to their expectations.

16:01.628 --> 16:04.664
An Abh who's worried about
what other people think?

16:04.664 --> 16:06.495
I've never met such an Abh.

16:07.000 --> 16:08.534
Yes. To tell you the truth...

16:08.534 --> 16:09.903
...I haven't either.

16:09.903 --> 16:10.536
But...

16:10.536 --> 16:13.072
...why make such a strong assertion?

16:13.072 --> 16:16.910
At any rate, you're being
unusually tough on me today.

16:16.910 --> 16:19.445
The reason may be that
the senior aviator...

16:19.445 --> 16:21.470
...hasn't seen me when I'm drunk.

16:22.882 --> 16:25.585
I'm sure I've seen you drunk before.

16:25.585 --> 16:27.553
You've probably seen me drinking.

16:27.553 --> 16:29.389
Not necessarily drunk.

16:29.389 --> 16:30.390
Is that so?

16:30.390 --> 16:32.790
And I'm to believe
you're drunk now?

16:33.326 --> 16:35.692
This is my second bottle, after all.

16:35.962 --> 16:38.231
Do you regularly drink this much?

16:38.231 --> 16:39.232
No.

16:39.232 --> 16:43.269
It's a luxury I allow myself
once a year.

16:43.269 --> 16:45.635
Normally, I just get a little tipsy.

16:46.639 --> 16:48.903
So, is today a special day?

16:52.345 --> 16:56.849
An enemy ten times our size will
be coming after us soon.

16:56.849 --> 16:59.875
That sort of thing doesn't happen
very often in your lifetime.

17:00.453 --> 17:01.487
True.

17:01.487 --> 17:03.456
If it happened often...

17:03.456 --> 17:06.550
...then there probably wouldn't
be much of a life left to live.

17:07.126 --> 17:08.593
Exactly!

17:16.069 --> 17:17.837
Once we get through the
next battle...

17:17.837 --> 17:20.567
...I'll buy you a bottle
of your favorite booze.

17:21.674 --> 17:23.509
That's very generous of you.

17:23.509 --> 17:25.912
I've heard that the senior aviator
is a wealthy woman...

17:25.912 --> 17:27.513
...so I won't hold back.

17:27.513 --> 17:29.949
I think that rumor's a bit
of an exaggeration.

17:29.949 --> 17:32.918
But you don't need to hold back.

17:34.120 --> 17:38.523
I've never been this happy pouring
my booze into someone else's glass!

17:40.860 --> 17:41.952
There are no reinforcements.

17:42.161 --> 17:45.062
But that was to be expected.

17:45.298 --> 17:46.822
This is our position here...

17:47.266 --> 17:49.635
Our mission is straightforward.

17:49.635 --> 17:52.229
We are to destroy the enemy.

17:52.438 --> 17:53.564
It's as simple as that.

17:53.706 --> 17:55.867
It sure sounds simple.

17:55.975 --> 17:59.911
But how long will we have to
keep it up for?

18:00.513 --> 18:01.514
Surely...

18:01.514 --> 18:04.950
...we can't keep hitting the enemy
for eternity.

18:05.785 --> 18:08.021
A maximum of 72 hours.

18:08.021 --> 18:10.990
That's what the command
has warned us to expect.

18:10.990 --> 18:14.357
There's nothing certain.
We'll have to take their word for it.

18:14.861 --> 18:17.163
I can't provide anything
more definite.

18:17.163 --> 18:21.156
After all, I'm merely
an assault unit commander.

18:21.968 --> 18:23.333
Any other questions?

18:28.574 --> 18:29.509
Very well.

18:29.509 --> 18:33.112
We will lose this battle if we let
the enemy through the gate.

18:33.112 --> 18:36.843
So we must do whatever it takes
to defend it with our lives.

18:36.983 --> 18:40.753
You can't worry about any
of the others within our unit.

18:40.753 --> 18:42.722
You might think this is easy...

18:42.722 --> 18:44.212
...but I do have my concerns.

18:44.824 --> 18:46.325
Some of you may...

18:46.325 --> 18:49.852
...go on to become admirals
and take command of a fleet.

18:49.996 --> 18:52.265
If that ever happens to you...

18:52.265 --> 18:54.358
...I want you never to forget
this feeling.

18:55.368 --> 18:57.003
Unit Commander...

18:57.003 --> 18:59.938
...don't you aspire to becoming
an Admiral of a fleet?

19:00.139 --> 19:00.969
Me?

19:01.107 --> 19:03.439
I think I'll pass on that, Captain.

19:03.576 --> 19:07.637
Just being in charge of a
remote unit is stressful enough.

19:08.047 --> 19:10.950
I don't want to be in command
of a whole fleet.

19:10.950 --> 19:13.186
The difference between
royalty and mere nobility...

19:13.186 --> 19:15.211
...is that we can be a little selfish.

19:15.855 --> 19:18.724
Oh, there's another difference.

19:18.724 --> 19:21.627
For royalty, holding territory
is an amusement to pass the time.

19:21.627 --> 19:22.495
However...

19:22.495 --> 19:26.090
...for us in the nobility,
the territories are our life.

19:26.299 --> 19:27.400
Could it be that...

19:27.400 --> 19:31.632
...she was aiming that comment
specifically at me?

19:32.939 --> 19:34.429
Time to change the subject.

19:35.608 --> 19:36.742
Senior Aviator...

19:36.742 --> 19:38.911
...what do you think of the captain?

19:38.911 --> 19:40.113
What do you mean?

19:40.113 --> 19:42.482
She sometimes seems out of whack.

19:42.482 --> 19:44.677
I mean, our captain's only nineteen!

19:44.817 --> 19:48.412
I don't think that's too young
to be captain of an attack ship.

19:48.721 --> 19:51.290
After all, one of the most
important qualities you need...

19:51.290 --> 19:52.358
...is sharp reflexes.

19:52.358 --> 19:55.194
No, I don't have any doubts
about her abilities.

19:55.194 --> 19:56.662
It's just that...

19:56.662 --> 20:00.433
...well, I've been working for the
Star Forces for twenty years now.

20:00.433 --> 20:02.935
Sometimes it makes me think.

20:02.935 --> 20:04.904
When I first joined the forces...

20:04.904 --> 20:08.806
...the captain had barely made it
out of the artificial womb.

20:09.242 --> 20:10.843
I'm sorry, but you've lost me.

20:10.843 --> 20:14.836
I can't figure out what
your problem is here.

20:15.781 --> 20:16.616
What?

20:16.616 --> 20:18.484
Just a drunk babbling away.

20:18.484 --> 20:21.654
But as to whether the captain
is the right person for the job...

20:21.654 --> 20:23.322
...I have a different opinion.

20:23.322 --> 20:24.223
Oh?

20:24.223 --> 20:26.418
Frankly, I'm a little
disappointed in her.

20:26.626 --> 20:30.926
You must know there are a lot of
legends about the Abriel family.

20:31.130 --> 20:33.690
Considering that, I'd say
the captain's pretty calm.

20:34.467 --> 20:36.536
You seriously think
she's calm?!

20:36.536 --> 20:39.338
More than I thought she would be.

20:39.338 --> 20:43.776
It seems to me that she feels
a little out of place here.

20:43.776 --> 20:47.678
Maybe she's not suited
to taking orders from above.

20:47.880 --> 20:50.183
They either need to give her
more power...

20:50.183 --> 20:53.452
...or maybe it would be better
if she acted alone.

20:53.452 --> 20:55.021
Out of place, huh?

20:55.021 --> 20:58.252
Come to think of it, that kid said
something along those lines.

20:59.759 --> 21:04.492
Maybe that's my problem, too.
I'm just feeling out of place.

21:05.431 --> 21:06.866
When I was a regular crewmember...

21:06.866 --> 21:08.734
...everyone was a Lander like me.

21:08.734 --> 21:11.202
Old, young, men, women...
all types of people.

21:12.038 --> 21:13.706
But up there on the bridge...

21:13.706 --> 21:16.008
...all I see are young Abh.

21:16.008 --> 21:18.578
I mean, you're actually
older than me...

21:18.578 --> 21:21.180
...but you still look like
a young lad, uh, I mean...

21:21.180 --> 21:23.444
Oops. Just a slip of the tongue.

21:24.083 --> 21:26.819
And the only other Lander around...

21:26.819 --> 21:30.255
...is not only young,
but he's even a count!

21:30.790 --> 21:32.519
It's just like...

21:34.427 --> 21:37.863
It's just like the Kulremen
Mountain mole.

21:37.863 --> 21:41.100
It's a saying from back home.

21:41.100 --> 21:45.638
There's a rocky outcrop
not far from where I lived...

21:45.638 --> 21:47.273
...called Kulremen Mountain.

21:47.273 --> 21:49.275
There was hardly any soil on it.

21:49.275 --> 21:52.011
When a mole tries to dig a hole...

21:52.011 --> 21:54.380
...it can't get very far.

21:54.380 --> 21:59.249
You can't do much about a rock
if you've got the nails of a mole.

21:59.752 --> 22:00.548
Sorry.

22:01.487 --> 22:02.221
That's okay.

22:02.221 --> 22:03.984
It doesn't bother me.

22:04.390 --> 22:05.224
However...

22:05.224 --> 22:08.318
...I hope you don't expect a reply!

22:09.262 --> 22:11.856
We've only drunk half the bottle.

22:12.098 --> 22:15.334
Let's save the other half
until after the battle.

22:15.334 --> 22:18.971
Unless all five of you are here,
this bottle won't be empty.

22:18.971 --> 22:21.040
Here's to your safe return!

22:21.040 --> 22:21.938
A toast!

22:25.378 --> 22:27.813
There's a lot to do before
the battle commences.

22:27.813 --> 22:29.081
The ceremony's over.

22:29.081 --> 22:29.979
Dismissed!

22:40.893 --> 22:43.462
Line Wing Aviator?
If you're going to sleep...

22:43.462 --> 22:45.865
...you should sleep
in your own room.

22:45.865 --> 22:49.402
Enemy Fleet
Expected to Arrive in...

22:49.402 --> 22:52.860
...24 hours

22:54.240 --> 22:58.540
kizukanaikoto ga
The things I did not notice

22:59.078 --> 23:03.344
konnani takusan aru
I didn't know there were so many

23:04.583 --> 23:08.280
kyoumade no jibun ga
I think of myself until today

23:09.522 --> 23:13.322
nasakenaku omoete
To be so pathetic

23:13.592 --> 23:15.561
kuyashii kurai
It's almost frustrating

23:15.561 --> 23:19.554
haritsumeta kimochiga
This tense feeling

23:20.766 --> 23:25.938
massugu ni muite ireba
As long as I keeping facing forward

23:25.938 --> 23:29.669
setsunasa no nukumori
This momentary warmth

23:29.909 --> 23:34.073
hajimete shitta
I understood it for the first time

23:34.613 --> 23:38.984
kimi ga iruto
When you are there

23:38.984 --> 23:46.192
itsumo pink no namida ga nagareteru
The pink tears are always flowing

23:46.192 --> 23:51.464
kono mune no naka wo afureteru
My heart is brimming with it

23:51.464 --> 24:00.031
kimi ga dokoni itemo dareto hanashitemo
Wherever you are and whoever you talk to

24:02.007 --> 24:07.146
issho ni itaiyo soba ni ite
I want to be with you, to be near you

24:07.146 --> 24:12.551
tsunaida te kara yubisaki kara
From our joined hands and our finger tips

24:12.551 --> 24:20.925
karadajuu no omoi binetsu tsutawatte
My body heat transmits the feelings inside

24:21.193 --> 24:25.630
tomerarenai
And I cannot stop it

24:31.971 --> 24:33.305
Close the hatches!

24:33.305 --> 24:35.207
Hatches closed!

24:35.207 --> 24:37.376
Prepare to separate gangways...

24:37.376 --> 24:38.411
...and to store them away.

24:38.411 --> 24:39.478
Preparations complete!

24:39.478 --> 24:42.379
Engage the forward
stabilizers with pulse drive!

24:42.581 --> 24:43.649
Commencing power!

24:43.649 --> 24:45.418
Separate gangways!

24:45.418 --> 24:46.552
Ignite engines!

24:46.552 --> 24:48.087
All engines fully operational!

24:48.087 --> 24:49.655
Ready for departure!

24:49.655 --> 24:50.956
The stabilizers are ready to go.

24:50.956 --> 24:52.321
Ignite the main engine!

24:52.758 --> 24:53.452
I repeat.

24:53.592 --> 24:56.220
The enemy fleet is expected
to enter range within six hours.

24:56.529 --> 24:57.897
All ships depart.

24:57.897 --> 24:58.330
Next Episode...
The Basroil's Battle

24:58.330 --> 24:59.765
Next Episode...
The Basroil's Battle
Daisiele!

24:59.765 --> 25:00.789
Next Episode...
The Basroil's Battle
